  "test_corrections": "Raw initial test compile E0597 and first baseline lifecycle repr mismatch retained. Callable handles hoisted outside evaluator loops; explicit GC uses nonspeculative fresh_string inputs and source-variable drop; final projection compares exact UTF-8 list values rather than assuming unescaped repr. Fresh corrected source-matched baseline shows two semantic passes / one intended pointer failure; candidate same tests pass. No production change to repair tests.",
  "limits": "Only unchanged ASCII uses input reuse; changed ASCII/all non-ASCII preserve original allocation path. Fixed2x98304-byte inputs have observed public Heap::allocated_bytes growth as recorded, not exact payload/Rust allocator count or general retained capacity/aggregate/peak/RSS/speed/source-fit benefit. Input ownership, metadata, fallback conversion and final heap/frozen storage remain. GC disabled only for isolated allocation/comparison probes; explicit GC/retained mutable results and functions tested separately.",
